IO-42: refuse a legacy hot start file with data left over; name short reads

HotStartManager::apply_legacy_routing() checks each read, but a short read
returned 1 without an error text, so the run stopped with "USE HOTSTART: "
and nothing else. It also never checked that the file ends where the model's
records end, so a file saved from a model with a storage unit where this model
has a junction (one float more) was applied with every later value shifted.
Set a message that covers every short read, and refuse a file with data left
over after the link records. Files that match the model are read as before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-42_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/HotStartManager.cpp b/src/engine/core/HotStartManager.cpp
index 29c8c0d..f8cdd3e 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/HotStartManager.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/HotStartManager.cpp
@@ -1317,6 +1317,10 @@ int HotStartManager::apply_legacy_routing(
         }
     }
 
+    // --- message for every short read below that does not set its own ---
+    tl_last_io_error = "Hotstart file '" + path +
+        "' ended before all records the model needs were read";
+
     // --- header object counts (legacy initializeFromHotstartFile) ---
     int32_t nSub = 0, nLand = 0, nNodes = 0, nLinks = 0, nPollut = 0, flowUnits = 0;
     if (version >= 2) { if (!read_pod(file, nSub))  return 1; } else nSub = ctx.n_subcatches();
@@ -1447,6 +1451,13 @@ int HotStartManager::apply_legacy_routing(
         for (int j = 0; j < nPollut; ++j) { float q = 0.0f; if (!read_pod(file, q)) return 1; }
     }
 
+    // --- data left over means the file does not match the model's layout ---
+    if (file.peek() != std::char_traits<char>::eof()) {
+        tl_last_io_error = "Hotstart file '" + path +
+            "' holds more data than the model's nodes and links need";
+        return 1;
+    }
+
     (void)flowUnits;
     (void)nLand;
     (void)warn_cb;
